course: dictionary
lesson: 1860
title: Cog: wheels, teeth and clever thinking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so use the words around it to find the right one. A cog is one of the teeth around the edge of a wheel. A whole toothed wheel is also called a cog or cogwheel. «Going up the steep hill to school, you click to a bigger back cog» is about a bike, so cog means a toothed wheel here.
explain: When a small cog turns a big cog, the big one turns more slowly but with more force. That is why a bike is easier to pedal up a hill. «Moving the chain to a bigger back cog makes pedalling easier but slower, good for hills.»
explain: Some meanings are pictures, not real wheels. «A cog in the machine» means a person with a small part in a big organisation who may feel unimportant. «The cogs were turning» means someone was thinking hard. Ask yourself: is this about real wheels, or is it a picture?
fact: A cog is one tooth on the edge of a wheel, and it fits between the teeth of another wheel.
fact: A cogwheel is a whole wheel with teeth around its edge, and it is also called a cog.
fact: «A cog in the machine» is a person with a small part in a big organisation who may feel unimportant.
fact: «The cogs were turning» means someone was thinking hard.
fact: In some places, UK slang «to cog» means to copy someone's homework.
exercise: «Moving the chain to a bigger back cog makes pedalling easier but slower.» What does cog mean in this sentence? | A loud noise from the chain | A type of homework | *A toothed wheel on the back of the bike | A pedal on the bike
exercise: «He is just a cog in the machine at the big firm.» What does cog mean here? | *A person with a small part who may feel unimportant | A type of bicycle chain | A toothed wheel inside a clock | A loud noise from the engine
exercise: «The cogs were turning as Sam solved the puzzle.» What does this mean? | *Sam was thinking hard | The machine was broken | Wheels were turning very fast | Sam was copying homework
test: «Your feet push the pedals, and the chain turns a small cog on the back wheel.» What is a cog in this sentence? | A bike seat | A brake | A pedal | *A toothed wheel that the chain turns
test: When a small cog turns a big cog, what happens? | It turns into a chain | It turns faster and with less force | *It turns more slowly but with more force | It stops moving
exam: Jayden says a cog is only one tooth. Is he completely right? | Yes, cogs are only for clocks | No, a cog is only a homework word | *No, a cog can be one tooth, and a whole toothed wheel can also be called a cog | Yes, a cog is never a whole wheel
